61,1762,1766,1771,1776,1780],{"id":277,"depth":933,"text":278},{"id":441,"depth":933,"text":236,"children":1763},[1764,1765],{"id":445,"depth":1013,"text":446},{"id":608,"depth":1013,"text":609},{"id":666,"depth":933,"text":256,"children":1767},[1768,1769,1770],{"id":672,"depth":1013,"text":673},{"id":732,"depth":1013,"text":733},{"id":949,"depth":1013,"text":950},{"id":1227,"depth":933,"text":1228,"children":1772},[1773,1774,1775],{"id":1245,"depth":1013,"text":1246},{"id":1379,"depth":1013,"text":1380},{"id":1473,"depth":1013,"text":1474},{"id":1512,"depth":933,"text":1513,"children":1777},[1778,1779],{"id":1637,"depth":1013,"text":1638},{"id":1668,"depth":1013,"text":1669},{"id":1741,"depth":933,"text":1742},"Feed Suricata and Wazuh alerts into Dodock Wolf, through the agent or the Wazuh integration, and find every source's events for one IP, host, site or user.","md",null,{},{"icon":43},{"title":158,"description":1781},"MCffFHyDnjMPQhu4Qj-eDmUUeCc8mf2p326YJiYFi0c",[1789,1791],{"title":154,"path":155,"stem":156,"description":1790,"icon":109},"Send Wolf's security events and signed journal to a syslog collector in OCSF or CEF, with the settings that work for rsyslog, Wazuh and Graylog.",{"title":168,"path":169,"stem":170,"description":1792,"icon":171},"Every endpoint, field and status code the Wolf Agent, satellites and integrations use to talk to the Wolf App (protocol v1).",1794994138762]